Bind the realtime gateway to loopback.

Upstream realtime/config/runtime.exs hard-codes the endpoint to every
interface (`ip: {0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0}`), so clients on the Cloudron
internal network could reach port 4000 directly, bypassing the internal
nginx and its HTTP/1.1-only, header-normalising proxy. In this package the
only client is that nginx (`upstream realtime { server 127.0.0.1:4000; }`)
and clustering is off (RELEASE_DISTRIBUTION=none), so the gateway listens on
127.0.0.1 like the API (HTTP_ADDR) and NATS (NATS_LISTEN). Drop this patch if
upstream makes the bind address configurable; then set it from start.sh.

--- a/realtime/config/runtime.exs
+++ b/realtime/config/runtime.exs
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@
 port = int.("PORT", 4000)
 
 config :realtime, RealtimeWeb.Endpoint,
-  http: [ip: {0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0}, port: port],
+  http: [ip: {127, 0, 0, 1}, port: port],
   secret_key_base: secret_key_base
 
 if config_env() == :test do
